===================

Moved out of LICENSE so that GitHub, F-Droid and other licence scanners can
detect the MIT licence. A LICENSE file with anything appended after the MIT
text is reported as NOASSERTION, which reads as "unlicensed" to tooling and
blocks F-Droid inclusion.

Twinlit's own code is MIT (see LICENSE). Twinlit is written from SunApp and MoonApp (both Stormberry AS,
MIT); the third-party parts they and Twinlit are built on are credited below. The build packages this
file inside the APK (assets/legal/NOTICE) and the footer's "Licences" link shows it, so that every
binary distribution carries it, which is what the licences of SunCalc and of the city data ask for.

